## Pre-flight
Tables: preflight.md (same directory). 10 findings; all rulings accepted:
- Ruling F1: pub(crate) items unused until a later task get `#[expect(dead_code, reason = "used from Task N")]`; the first-using task removes it — clippy -D warnings must pass per commit — cost if wrong: noise only.
- Ruling F2: Task 7 ResumePlan records the transfer call id per path level, adds `transfer_call_to_next() -> Option<&str>`, test asserts `t1` — search by name breaks with a custom HandoffDef::tool_name — cost: one accessor.
- Ruling F3: the agent that denies (renamed root, or missing target at any level) closes EVERY transfer call after its level with "agent no longer available: {name}"; Task 8b adds tests for renamed root on a multi-agent path and missing middle agent on a path of three — spec §2 valid-request goal — cost: two tests.
- Ruling F4: drop the `skip` parameter of assert_tool_calls_paired.
- Ruling F5: accept the helper copy in runtime-tokio tests, comment on each copy naming the other.
- Ruling F6: Task 11 adds private `restrict_unsupported_run_features` in runtime-temporal plus unit tests (flag cleared, warning path).
- Ruling F7: `recheck_counts_ask_user_as_answered` uses no handler.
- Ruling F8: ResumePlan gets a manual Debug that hides args.
- Ruling F9: task text and its commit command are the file authority, not the file map; Task 2 may touch graph.rs.
- Ruling F10: PathTooDeep test defers with default depth, resumes with max_agent_depth = 0.

